# Bounded US menu-navigation diagnostic (r481, settle fix r483). Extends
# us-pretype28-startup.steps through the game-data-browser selection screen,
# to probe whether a highlighted/selected menu cursor draws with a different
# primitive_type than the static title screen. Stops before any
# hangar/deploy/gameplay step.
#
# r482 tried making this preamble byte-identical to us-pretype28-startup's
# (which reliably succeeds) -- still stalled identically, ruling out route
# content matching that route as the fix (see r482's report).
#
# r483: the mission01-qualified-96.steps sealed route's own literal first
# steps (key Escape 0.1 / sleep 2 / key space 0.1 / wait-pulse type28=30
# Escape+space -- the same pattern r482's byte-identical preamble used) are
# the pattern run_gate.py's mission_cinematic_handoff / mission_render_summary
# special case explicitly REPLACES before running (tools/run_gate.py:745-756)
# -- its own comment documents that firing the Escape/space pulse
# immediately, before the renderer/movie workers settle, can "straddle the
# movie transition" and stop presentation. --dump_shaders (added r481) does
# not apply that override, so this probe inherited the flaky raw pattern.
# Fixed here by using the DIFFERENT settle-then-Escape-only-pulse shape
# run_gate.py's own override already uses (not literal identity with either
# existing route) -- verified end to end (clean_shutdown, game_status=0,
# all three captures, translatable shader cache). One successful run is not
# proof against r482's documented cycle-time variance; re-verify before
# relying on this route being reliable.
sleep	20
capture	post-settle
wait-pulse	type28=30	Escape@90
capture	type28-30
sleep	1
key	space	0.1
wait	type28=[^ ]*37	20
key	Left	0.1
key	space	0.1
wait	type28=[^ ]*35	20
key	space	0.1
wait	selector44=[^ ]*3	20
capture	game-data-browser
